137>>425756391\n>>425755924\nI'd say Light Bowgun is the easiest ranged weapon to use, since it's just about managing ammo and positioning, while the Heavy Bowgun can dish out more damage but needs better positioning and Bow needs stamina management. As for most skilled, I'd say Switch Axe because of its various modes and big risk-reward gameplay.\n\nAnonymous 04/12/23(Wed)16:24:52 No.425756391>>425756543\n>>425756137\nSwitch Axe is definitely up there in terms of skill ceiling, but I still think Hunting Horn and Insect Glaive have it beat because of their support/utility aspects. As for ranged weapons, I agree that Light Bowgun is easiest and Bow has the most skill involved, but I don't think Heavy Bowgun is too far off from Bow in terms of difficulty.\n\nAnonymous 04/12/23(Wed)16:27:09 No.425756543\n>>425756391\nSo, let's say the hardest to master are Hunting Horn, Insect Glaive, and Switch Axe, while the easiest to pick up are Sword and Shield, Charge Blade, and Light Bowgun? Sounds about right.\n\nAnonymous 04/12/23(Wed)16:29:32 No.425756728\nYeah, I'd agree with that assessment. Of course, everyone's experience with each weapon may differ, but overall that seems to be the general consensus.\n\nRemember that every weapon is viable in the right hands, and it's just a matter of finding what you enjoy playing the most. Happy hunting, folks!", "country": null, "hashed_ip": null, "header": null, "language": "English", "redacted": false, "role": "assistant", "state": null, "timestamp": "2023-04-12 21:32:03+00:00", "toxic": false, "turn_identifier": 132680}], "turn": 1, "language": "English", "openai_moderation": [{"categories": {"harassment": false, "harassment/threatening": false, "harassment_threatening": false, "hate": false, "hate/threatening": false, "hate_threatening": false, "self-harm": false, "self-harm/instructions": false, "self-harm/intent": false, "self_harm": false, "self_harm_instructions": false, "self_harm_intent": false, "sexual": false, "sexual/mino