ation):\n    print(f\"Individual {i}: {ind}\")\n```\n\nAs you requested, I've divided the code into 3 sections:\n\n1. **Section 1: Functions** - This section contains all the functions required for the genetic algorithm, such as rastrigin(), fitness(), initialize_population(), selection(), crossover(), and mutation().\n2. **Section 2: Evolution** - This section is responsible for running the genetic algorithm itself, initializing the population, and executing the main loop for the specified number of generations.\n3. **Section 3: Results** - This section prints the best solution found and the final population after the specified generations.\n\nTo adjust the population size, simply change the value of the `population_size` variable at the top of the code, and the algorithm will use that value for the initial population size.\n\nConverting the code to a Jupyter Notebook (ipynb) is straightforward. Simply create a new Jupyter Notebook, and copy each section of the code into separate cells, running the cells in order after copying the code. This will keep the same structure and organization, making it easy to understand and modify in the Jupyter Notebook format.", "country": null, "hashed_ip": null, "header": null, "language": "English", "redacted": false, "role": "assistant", "state": null, "timestamp": "2023-04-12 21:07:21+00:00", "toxic": false, "turn_identifier": 132589}, {"content": "Is it possible we can combine the settings and problem parameters into 1 which are maybe under config? because i think those are settings that we can configure in order to optimize the problem. And also would you mind adding markdown about explanation or something to your liking. ", "country": "Malaysia", "hashed_ip": "e9543bcac99dd513a3872537876be8231ba79e8d5516400ce7a0a585cbe8d8fd", "header": {"accept-language": "en-US,en;q=0.9", "user-agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/111.0.0.0 Safari/537.36"}, "language": "English", "r