{"conversation_hash": "c3949a0e088f3e85af515972cb3a1007", "model": "gpt-4-0314", "timestamp": "2023-04-12 22:17:22+00:00", "conversation": [{"content": "write me a sql file based on these instructions: Enhancement #1 – Better Inventory Tracking\nThe existing database has three fields in the Products table that are currently used to track inventory stock (UnitsInStock, UnitsOnOrder, ReorderLevel). However, the company owns three different warehouses, and currently has no way of tracking stock levels for each product in each warehouse. Inventory for any product could be stored at any of the three warehouse locations. Each warehouse has a name and a street address that should be stored in the new database. The warehouses are commonly known by their location within the city: The Dockside warehouse, the Airport warehouse and the Central warehouse. The new scheme should be able to record the same basic data as the existing database (UnitsInStock, UnitsOnOrder, ReorderLevel), but also reference the warehouse in which the products are currently being stored in, or re-ordered from. Note: Your script should distribute existing products amongst the three warehouses. Feel free to make up the distribution.\n\nEnhancement #2 – Full Names with Title\n\nThe HR department has requested a database change to help integration with the new HR software program. The new software does not work well when importing separate values for first/last names and the title of courtesy. They propose adding a new field that contains a combined value in the following format: <Courtesy Title> <First Name> <Last Name>. Examples: Mr. John Doe or Dr. Jane Smith. The proposed field will not replace the usage of the existing separate fields; it will simply be a redundant field containing the full value from the three other fields, for use only with the new HR software program.\n\nDeliverable Descriptions & Requirements\nDatabase Setup & Requirements\n\nFor this project, you will need to create one new database:\n\nCreate a new, empty database named exactly: northwind_Enhanced. This db represents the “new and improved” db you will give your client upon completion of all work and testing.\n\nAfter the initial database creation, no structural or data changes (DDL or DML) should occur in the original Northwind database.", "country": "Canada", "hashed_ip": "f48dbd9cd788089d2c80f5ba1cf89095ce6ee8cce65a3f43f5a3cfa453689781", "header": {"accept-language": "en-US,en;q=0.9", "user-agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/112.0.0.0 Safari/537.36 Edg/112.0.1722.34"}, "language": "English", "redacted": false, "role": "user", "state": "Nova Scotia", "timestamp": null, "toxic": false, "turn_identifier": 132789}, {"content": "-- SQL File for Enhancements\n\n-- Enhancement #1 – Better Inventory Tracking\n\n-- Create Warehouses table\nCREATE TABLE Warehouses (\n  WarehouseID INT PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  WarehouseName VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,\n  StreetAddress VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL\n);\n\n-- Insert warehouse data\nINSERT INTO Warehouses (WarehouseName, StreetAddress)\nVALUES ('Dockside warehouse', '123 Dockside St'),\n       ('Airport warehouse', '456 Airport Rd'),\n       ('Central warehouse', '789 Central Ave');\n\n-- Create ProductWarehouses table\nCREATE TABLE ProductWarehouses (\n  ProductID INT NOT NULL,\n  WarehouseID INT NOT NULL,\n  UnitsInStock INT,\n  UnitsOnOrder INT,\n  ReorderLevel INT,\n  FOREIGN KEY (ProductID) REFERENCES Products(ProductID),\n  FOREIGN KEY (WarehouseID) REFERENCES Warehouses(WarehouseID)\n);\n\n-- Sample distribution of existing products among the warehouses\nINSERT INTO ProductWarehouses (ProductID, WarehouseID, UnitsInStock, UnitsOnOrder, ReorderLevel)\nSELECT ProductID, (ProductID % 3) + 1, UnitsInStock, UnitsOnOrder, ReorderLevel\nFROM Products;\n\n-- Enhancement #2 – Full Names with Title\n\n-- Add FullNameWithTitle column to Employees table\nALTER TABLE Employees\nADD FullNameWithTitle VARCHAR(255);\n\n-- Update FullNameWithTitle with the format: <Courtesy Title> <First Name> <Last Name>\nUPDATE Employees\nSET FullNameWithTitle = CONCAT(TitleOfCourtesy, ' ', FirstName, ' ', LastName);\n\n-- Create northwind_Enhanced database\nCREATE DATABASE northwind_Enhanced;\n\n-- Copy existing tables and data from Northwind to northwind_Enhanced\nUSE northwind_Enhanced;\n\nCREATE TABLE Customers AS SELECT * FROM Northwind.Customers;\nCREATE TABLE Categories AS SELECT * FROM Northwind.Categories;\nCREATE TABLE Employees AS SELECT * FROM Northwind.Employees;\nCREATE TABLE Shippers AS SELECT * FROM Northwind.Shippers;\nCREATE TABLE Suppliers AS SELECT * FROM Northwind.Suppliers;\nCREATE TABLE Orders AS SELECT * FROM Northwind.Orders;\nCREATE TABLE Products AS SELECT * FROM Northwind.Products;\nCREATE TABLE OrderDetails AS SELECT * FROM Northwind.OrderDetails;\n\n-- Apply enhancements on the northwind_Enhanced database\nUSE northwind_Enhanced;\n\nALTER TABLE Employees\nADD FullNameWithTitle VARCHAR(255);\n\nUPDATE Employees\nSET FullNameWithTitle = CONCAT(TitleOfCourtesy, ' ', FirstName, ' ', LastName);\n\nCREATE TABLE Warehouses (\n  WarehouseID INT PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  WarehouseName VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,\n  StreetAddress VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL\n);\n\nINSERT INTO Warehouses (WarehouseName, StreetAddress)\nVALUES ('Dockside warehouse', '123 Dockside St'),\n       ('Airport warehouse', '456 Airport Rd'),\n       ('Central warehouse', '789 Central Ave');\n\nCREATE TABLE ProductWarehouses (\n  ProductID INT NOT NULL,\n  WarehouseID INT NOT NULL,\n  UnitsInStock INT,\n  UnitsOnOrder INT,\n  ReorderLevel INT,\n  FOREIGN KEY (ProductID) REFERENCES Products(ProductID),\n  FOREIGN KEY (WarehouseID) REFERENCES Warehouses(WarehouseID)\n);\n\nINSERT INTO ProductWarehouses (ProductID, WarehouseID, UnitsInStock, UnitsOnOrder, ReorderLevel)\nSELECT ProductID, (ProductID % 3) + 1, UnitsInStock, UnitsOnOrder, ReorderLevel\nFROM Products;", "country": null, "hashed_ip": null